The `main` lane is served by `big` and then by `small`. A lane is a role on a
substrate, fixed for the run; a lane that changes substrate is two lanes, and
the record should say so by naming two.

The cost of allowing it lands on `rejected`, which carries a lane and no
substrate of its own. Its substrate is its lane's, by reference -- one fact,
written once. A lane with two substrates would give that reference two
answers, and then the row would need its own copy of a fact the lane already
holds.
